docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4299:### G16: DNSSEC algorithm and validation profile — NARROW-CLAIM (visible owner scope choice)
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4307:- **Supported set (owner scope choice).** DNSKEY and RRSIG algorithms 8 (RSA/SHA-256, RFC 5702, key per RFC 3110)
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4320:  | Else, an unsupported algorithm or digest type could supply the required path | `UNVERIFIABLE / DNSSEC_ALGORITHM_UNSUPPORTED` |
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4329:- **Rationale.** The live chain is root and `com` at algorithm 8, wamason.com at 13, and DS type 2 at both
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4330:  delegations (SPIKE-REPORT). RFC 4035 would treat an unsupported algorithm as insecure; V1 must never let that pass.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4333:- **Visible limit.** A chain that moves to an algorithm outside {8, 13} (for example a TLD or root move to Ed25519,
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4334:  algorithm 15) makes new snapshots `UNVERIFIABLE` under this frozen spec. *Withdrawn example (2026-10-14):* "a root
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4335:  move to ECDSA" was wrong, since algorithm 13 is already supported; a new unlisted KSK is a separate trust-coverage
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4393:  and other root algorithms may be rejected; that limit is visible.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4394:- **OPEN, owner act.** The deployed repository-root algorithm is not yet demonstrated: YubiKey 2 is not in hand.
docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:4395:  Confirm P-256 before the freeze; if another algorithm is used, list that one instead and add it to G15.
