docs/reviews/v1-profile-r2/codex.log:5211:| G16 / DNSSEC algorithm and validation profile | Which exact DNSSEC algorithms/editions, canonical signed-data rules, delegation handling and unsupported-algorithm outcomes govern? | `docs/V1-PROFILE.md:290-295`, `:398-407`, `:436`; `docs/phase-0-prereg-amendment-9.md:141`, `:158`, `:307-323` | **Silent here / external dependency.** Root existential rule and selected witness timing are concrete, but the full DNSSEC verifier profile and normative dependency closure are absent. | Stop; no network/RFC lookup or library used to fill policy. An algorithm in the historical chain supported by one validator and unsupported by another changes performability; an extra invalid RRSIG must not defeat a valid witness (P:403-406 resolves that part). | **yes** |
